  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently \"isCollection\" is not present in the Fedora relationships ontology at ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora-commons.org/definitions/1/0/fedora-relsext-ontology.rdfs"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora-commons.org/definitions/1/0/fedora-relsext-ontology.rdfs",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ".  However it's a term that does seem to get used fairly frequently to allow discovery of resources that have children.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "See the recent post by Gill Hamilton to the users list.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The wiki page FAQ item on this does in fact use this predicate although it is not defined in the ontology (",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=17530955)"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=17530955)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " and Muradora also made use of this undefined predicate.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Should we therefore consider updating the ontology to include this?  Or should we recommend that people use a predicate from their own namespace (and update the wiki FAQ item also)?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
