     },
     "body": "<p>No, we do not need a third way of expressing the type of an object. #hasModel is the way to express the class of an object. Yes, you can use rdf:type. And yes, you can use dc. But these are non-standard in a fedora context.</p>\n\n<p>About collection objects. No, let's not go there. We should not add a \"Collection\" content model. There are numerous reasons why this would be a bad idea. And without a specific content models, we should not add a \"isPartOfCollection\" relation to the ontology</p>",
     "created": "09/Aug/10 10:10 AM",
     "id": "11507",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10703/comment/11507",
